WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.964 --> 00:00:17.508
The next day Julia and Markos went to the gymnasium to watch Brody's training, as usual.

2
00:00:17.528 --> 00:00:22.770
"Wow, there are lots of gods here today," Julia said.

3
00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:24.991
Markos nodded.

4
00:00:25.011 --> 00:00:29.592
"As the Games draw closer, the gods become quite focused on the competition.

5
00:00:31.268 --> 00:00:34.389
Only the most powerful gods have a real chance of winning, of course.

6
00:00:35.949 --> 00:00:38.210
But the others don't want to make it easy for them!"

7
00:00:40.051 --> 00:00:41.391
Julia looked at the field.

8
00:00:43.031 --> 00:00:48.553
She couldn't help worrying about whether Brody would be good enough to compete against all these other athletes.

9
00:00:50.393 --> 00:00:53.934
Still, she could tell that he was doing his best to train hard.

10
00:00:55.355 --> 00:00:59.456
She watched Hermes hand Brody a discus and then gesture toward the course.

11
00:01:01.372 --> 00:01:07.456
As Julia followed the track of Brody's toss, she noticed Ares creeping along the edge of the field.

12
00:01:07.476 --> 00:01:10.298
"What's Ares doing?"

13
00:01:10.898 --> 00:01:11.379
she said.

14
00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:14.501
Markos glanced at the god of war.

15
00:01:14.521 --> 00:01:18.463
"Probably trying to sabotage another god's champion."

16
00:01:20.004 --> 00:01:22.966
"You mean like what Hera and Aphrodite tried to do to Brody?"

17
00:01:23.447 --> 00:01:24.367
Julia asked.

18
00:01:25.768 --> 00:01:27.690
"Do the gods do that kind of thing a lot?"

19
00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:31.092
"Of course," Markos replied.

20
00:01:31.852 --> 00:01:34.173
"Ares has quite a rivalry with Apollo.

21
00:01:35.773 --> 00:01:39.094
He's not eager to have his sister Athena beat him in the Games either.

22
00:01:40.614 --> 00:01:43.775
Oh, and I heard he recently quarreled with Hephaestus."

23
00:01:45.096 --> 00:01:46.056
Julia shivered.

24
00:01:46.776 --> 00:01:49.157
"The gods really can't be trusted, can they?"

25
00:01:49.657 --> 00:01:50.177
she said.

26
00:01:50.197 --> 00:01:53.798
"What if they keep trying to sabotage Brody?"

27
00:01:53.818 --> 00:01:56.198
"They probably will."

28
00:01:56.879 --> 00:01:57.759
Markos shrugged.

29
00:01:57.779 --> 00:02:01.620
"Then we should do something to help him."

30
00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.021
Julia stood up.

31
00:02:04.402 --> 00:02:08.266
She was tired of sitting around watching Brody run and jump and throw things.

32
00:02:09.687 --> 00:02:12.410
"Let's go spy on the other gods and their champions.

33
00:02:13.931 --> 00:02:16.834
Maybe we can figure out which ones are the biggest threat to Brody."

34
00:02:18.656 --> 00:02:21.258
Markos looked surprised, but he stood up too.

35
00:02:21.278 --> 00:02:23.881
"That's a good idea.

36
00:02:24.301 --> 00:02:27.324
The gods usually can't help bragging about their tricks and plans.

37
00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:33.512
If we listen carefully, we might be able to help Brody stay safe—and even win."

38
00:02:36.614 --> 00:02:37.834
"Where are you two going?"

39
00:02:38.475 --> 00:02:41.617
Brody called out as Julia and Markos headed for an exit.

40
00:02:43.198 --> 00:02:44.359
Hermes looked over too.

41
00:02:44.379 --> 00:02:49.062
"We're, uh, going to the agora."

42
00:02:49.562 --> 00:02:50.503
Markos flushed.

43
00:02:50.523 --> 00:02:55.126
"My mother asked me to get some extra eels for tonight's dinner."

44
00:02:56.667 --> 00:02:57.908
Hermes smacked his lips.

45
00:02:58.780 --> 00:02:59.480
"Eels, eh?"

46
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:00.501
he said.

47
00:03:00.521 --> 00:03:01.901
"My favorite!

48
00:03:02.241 --> 00:03:03.481
Make sure you get plenty, boy.

49
00:03:04.802 --> 00:03:08.703
We'll meet you at the agora when we're finished here in case you need help carrying them."

50
00:03:10.564 --> 00:03:12.944
"How many eels does Hermes expect you to get?"

51
00:03:13.505 --> 00:03:15.925
Julia whispered as she and Markos hurried out.

52
00:03:15.945 --> 00:03:19.466
"It doesn't matter," Markos said.

53
00:03:19.486 --> 00:03:21.867
"I just made that up about my mother.

54
00:03:22.867 --> 00:03:24.748
Let's go to the agora and see who's there."

55
00:03:26.992 --> 00:03:30.573
A few minutes later, the two kids were wandering around the agora.

56
00:03:31.413 --> 00:03:32.794
As usual, it was crowded.

57
00:03:33.814 --> 00:03:37.175
A fabric merchant was placing a bolt of silk in front of his tent.

58
00:03:38.655 --> 00:03:42.776
Two farmers were arguing loudly over the price of a flock of honking geese.

59
00:03:44.617 --> 00:03:48.078
Several small boys dodged through the crowd toward another stall.

60
00:03:49.258 --> 00:03:52.519
There were only a few gods in view, including Hera.

61
00:03:52.539 --> 00:03:58.129
"Let's go closer," Julia whispered, nodding at the queen of the gods.

62
00:03:59.709 --> 00:04:05.611
Julia and Markos moved toward Hera, who was talking to her champion, a muscular young man with a

63
00:04:05.651 --> 00:04:06.671
scar on his cheek.

64
00:04:08.132 --> 00:04:13.153
and you'll have to do much better at the long jump," the goddess was saying when Julia got

65
00:04:13.213 --> 00:04:14.093
close enough to hear.

66
00:04:14.113 --> 00:04:21.996
"Because my husband has been bragging that his champion once leaped across the Elpeus River at its widest

67
00:04:22.096 --> 00:04:25.556
point." "Do you think that's true?"

68
00:04:26.077 --> 00:04:27.537
Julia whispered to Markos.

69
00:04:29.358 --> 00:04:31.738
"I don't know," Markos whispered back.

70
00:04:32.699 --> 00:04:34.959
"Nobody in Olympia has seen Alcides."

71
00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:39.901
Julia noticed a pair of gods striding into the agora.

72
00:04:39.921 --> 00:04:43.462
"Look! Artemis and Apollo.

73
00:04:44.002 --> 00:04:45.322
Let's spy on them for a while!"

74
00:04:48.563 --> 00:04:54.475
After eavesdropping on some of the gods, Julia was feeling more confident about Brody's chances in the Games.

75
00:04:55.856 --> 00:05:00.700
She and Markos had also spoken to three or four mortal champions who happened to pass by.

76
00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:08.086
"It sounds like Brody actually has a good chance of beating most of the athletes in most of

77
00:05:08.126 --> 00:05:09.847
the events," Julia said.

78
00:05:09.867 --> 00:05:13.330
"But I'm worried about two things."

79
00:05:15.211 --> 00:05:17.253
"Alcides?" Markos guessed.

80
00:05:17.273 --> 00:05:20.636
"Of course," Julia replied.

81
00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:25.283
"As you said, nobody will know what he's like until he shows up.

82
00:05:25.723 --> 00:05:27.745
I'm also worried about the chariot race."

83
00:05:27.765 --> 00:05:30.928
"Why?" Markos asked.

84
00:05:30.948 --> 00:05:34.771
"That event doesn't usually require much athletic ability."

85
00:05:36.272 --> 00:05:37.173
Julia frowned.

86
00:05:37.193 --> 00:05:39.215
"It requires skill.

87
00:05:39.775 --> 00:05:43.599
And as far as I know, Brody has never even seen a horse up close.

88
00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:47.002
He might be terrible at driving them.

89
00:05:47.542 --> 00:05:52.513
I think I'll try to convince Hermes to—" A loud shout suddenly interrupted her.

90
00:05:53.914 --> 00:05:58.395
Suddenly everyone in the agora was turning around, peering in the same direction.

91
00:05:58.415 --> 00:06:00.917
"What's going on?"

92
00:06:01.397 --> 00:06:02.237
Julia asked.

93
00:06:03.738 --> 00:06:07.559
Markos stood on tiptoes, trying to see what everyone was looking at.

94
00:06:07.579 --> 00:06:10.261
"Oh!" he said.

95
00:06:10.281 --> 00:06:11.861
"It's Zeus."

96
00:06:13.302 --> 00:06:18.024
Just then an enormous figure leaped onto a dais in the center of the agora.

97
00:06:19.292 --> 00:06:22.793
Julia would have known that it was Zeus even if Markos hadn't said so.

98
00:06:24.734 --> 00:06:28.355
Zeus looked just as she had imagined the king of the gods to look.

99
00:06:30.515 --> 00:06:34.276
He appeared huge and powerful, with a long gray beard.

100
00:06:34.296 --> 00:06:39.098
"Attention, people of Olympia!"

101
00:06:40.818 --> 00:06:43.299
Zeus' voice boomed out over the agora.

102
00:06:43.319 --> 00:06:47.360
"I have a very important announcement."

103
00:06:48.524 --> 00:06:52.166
The agora went silent except for the sounds of animals and birds.

104
00:06:53.707 --> 00:06:57.089
Out of the corner of her eye, Julia suddenly saw movement.

105
00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:02.932
Turning, she noticed Hermes pushing his way forward with Brody at his heels.

106
00:07:04.433 --> 00:07:07.195
They were staring up at Zeus just like everyone else.

107
00:07:07.215 --> 00:07:09.836
"What is it, Zeus?"

108
00:07:10.357 --> 00:07:11.377
Hermes called out.

109
00:07:11.397 --> 00:07:13.238
"Don't keep us in suspense."

110
00:07:15.159 --> 00:07:16.000
Zeus smiled.

111
00:07:16.968 --> 00:07:24.095
"I know you've all been eagerly awaiting the chance to cast your eyes upon Alcides," he said.

112
00:07:24.115 --> 00:07:27.558
"Soon your wait will be over.

113
00:07:29.139 --> 00:07:38.068
Alcides—the most impressive mortal champion in all of Greece—arrives in Olympia in just two more days!"
